<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Batu Tarsilah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1807">1807</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Batu Tarsilah is an inscribed stone tablet in Brunei, set up in 1807 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Muhammad Tajuddin, recording in Malay in Jawi script the genealogy of the sultans of Brunei. Together with written genealogies such as the Salasilah Raja-Raja Brunei, it is a principal source for the traditional order of Brunei's rulers, from the first sultan Muhammad Shah onwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/batu-tarsilah.jpg" alt="Batu Tarsilah" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pangalau · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batu_Tarsilah_at_the_Brunei_Royal_Mausoleum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
